==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
Named after Brazilian physician [[w:Carlos Chagas|Carlos Chagas]] (1879-1934), who first described it in 1909.

===Pronunciation===
{{rfp|en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|head=[[Chagas]]' [[disease]]|-}}

# {{lb|en|disease}} A form of [[trypanosomiasis]] prevalent in [[South America]], caused by the parasitic [[trypanosome]] ''{{w|T. cruzi}}''. It is transmitted to many [[mammal]]s such as [[human]]s through [[insect]] bites, mainly by [[kissing bug]]s. Symptoms include [[fever]], [[oedema]], [[cardiomyopathy]], and enlargement of the [[spleen]] and [[lymph node]]s. It can be [[fatal]].

